  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec\\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[arcsec({e}^{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u206110$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{\u2032}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u206110) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(10)/2)}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
